  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Banque Misr SL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFC&apos;s proposed investment in Banque Misr (BM or the Bank) consists of (i) an up to US$150 million 3-year investment in the form of a senior sustainability loan. This investment forms part of a broader IFC Board-approved investment envelope of up to US$220 million, with any additional amount subject to further considerations and approvals.&#xa0;The proceeds will be&#xa0; directed to support the Bank&apos;s lending activities to green and sustainable projects with 50% directed to climate assets, with 30% of that amount dedicated to funding the banks own green buildings. 50% to micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) including a 20% carveout to women owned MSMEs (WMSMEs); and (ii) an uncommitted trade finance facility under IFC Global Trade Finance Program (GTFP) (the Project).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The most significant expected project-level outcome is increased access to climate finance, and MSME finance including WMSMEs in Egypt. Beyond the Project, IFC anticipates that the Project will foster greater sustainability in the market through demonstration and replication channels by showcasing the commercial viability of lending to climate assets.</narrative>
  </description>
